      </categoryLinks>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Wintergrave Siege Terminators" id="ad06-fd95-9dcc-3c86" hidden="false" typeId="0cb1-7394-fb88-5322" typeName="Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="M" typeId="8ffa-8367-2184-5557">5"</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="c2bc-ad63-c63b-5cea">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="f078-5176-43c6-5f6a">2+</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="ecdc-11e1-15d1-5780">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="2bb6-cceb-9d3f-5f47">6+</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="OC" typeId="6bb9-f7e0-3ec4-5517">1 (2 Prepared)</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Invulnerable" typeId="fcc9-7d25-7e12-9146">4+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Unrestricted Arsenal" id="5fe1-28a8-6473-ea31" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">Each model may fire its modular siege missile launcher and all other eligible ranged weapons in the same Shooting phase. A single combi-weapon or launcher may fire only one of its modes at a time.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Wintergrave Bastion Protocol" id="49d7-724a-532f-4716" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">After objective control is checked at the end of your Movement phase, if this unit remained stationary this phase and controls an objective, establish Prepared Strongpoint there. While established: OC2, Benefit of Cover, and re-roll missile Hit rolls of 1 versus targets within 6" of defended objective. Any actual move by any model or loss of objective breaks it. Terrain objectives measured to nearest terrain-area boundary.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Wintergrave Master Protocol" id="ee22-b741-04b7-9a7d" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">While prepared and Siege-Master alive, select one at end of your Movement phase: Frostsight (once per Shooting phase re-roll one missile Wound roll vs enemy within 12" of objective); Icebound (re-roll one failed saving throw per phase); Winter's Retribution (+1 melee Hit versus unit charging prepared position while still fortified). One at a time. Death of Siege-Master cancels protocol.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Frostforged Targeting Matrix" id="e25c-bd63-5eab-3e35" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">At start of Shooting phase while prepared, each targeting coordinator can designate a different visible enemy within 24" of itself; choose Ignores Cover or ignore negative Hit roll modifiers for this unit's attacks against that designated target. No duplicate targets or stacking.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Wintergrave Continuity Protocol" id="e231-8ac2-1e1a-2a7d" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">Any move by any attached/organic model including forced moves, pile-in and consolidation ends Prepared Strongpoint. Casualty removal alone does not. Siege-Master death ends Master Protocol, not Bastion. An attached Leader cannot replace Siege-Master.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Specialist Quotas (important)" id="696e-fe69-f308-bc15" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">Per squad: for 5–9 models up to 1 specialist payload, 1 secondary heavy weapon and 1 coordinator; for 10 models up to 2 of each. No model may have all three categories; at most one convergence beam per squad. The offline Wintergrave roster editor and external Python validator fully enforce these cross-model totals; XML app-specific cross-parent checks are subject to New Recruit import verification.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Glacierbreaker" id="0250-3995-de65-b6bf" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">Anti-Fortification 4+ against FORTIFICATION only .</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Frostshard Suppression" id="af94-537b-953d-aeda" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">while prepared, Frostshard Hits against INFANTRY/BEASTS/SWARM within 12" of defended objective impose -1 ranged Hit rolls on target until start of your next Shooting phase; nonstacking.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Blackice Disruption" id="1014-32d4-756b-5882" hidden="false" typeId="bd5c-f804-35b5-510d" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="4c71-0d90-3b92-5cec">after unsaved Blackice wound, enemy cannot re-roll ranged Hit rolls against this Wintergrave unit until start of your next Shooting phase; nonstacking.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
